    <item>
      <title>Sem Legenda nas Falas Dubladas (Dublagem PT-BR)</title>
      <author>gabee404</author>
      <link>https://gamebanana.com/mods/726064</link>
      <comments>https://gamebanana.com/mods/726064#PostsListModule</comments>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">fa584a9ea0366f1b475a6f2b7db498fc364b6e7d</guid>
      <pubDate>Sat, 10 Oct 2026 05:57:50 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ac9d3c325580.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ac9d3c58caa6.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Qual é a desse mod?&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
Cansou de ficar lendo legenda enquanto o personagem tá literalmente falando com você? Pois é, eu também ?&lt;br&gt;Esse mod &lt;b&gt;tira a legenda SÓ das falas que têm voz&lt;/b&gt;, deixando as cutscenes muito mais cinematográficas. O resto continua igualzinho.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;O que ele faz&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;❌ Tira a legenda de &lt;b&gt;1.230 falas dubladas&lt;/b&gt;: cutscenes da história, memórias, gritos dos sábios em batalha (Tulin, Yunobo, Riju, Sidon...), avisos tipo "faltam só 2!" e por aí vai&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;✅ Falas sem voz e caixas de diálogo (aquelas que você aperta A pra passar) continuam com texto, então você não perde nada&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;✅ Menus, itens, missões: tudo normal&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;? &lt;b&gt;NÃO&lt;/b&gt; mexe em nenhum áudio nem na dublagem&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;? Funciona com o jogo em &lt;b&gt;Português do Brasil&lt;/b&gt; e em &lt;b&gt;Inglês (EUA)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Requisitos&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOTK versão 1.4.3&lt;/b&gt; (NÃO funciona em outras versões, os arquivos de texto mudam a cada update)&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Feito pra usar junto com a &lt;b&gt;dublagem PT-BR da Triforce Heroes&lt;/b&gt;. Sem a dublagem, algumas falas que não têm voz no jogo original também vão ficar sem legenda.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Como instalar (Ryujinx)&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&lt;ol&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Baixa o zip&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;No Ryujinx, clica com o botão direito no &lt;b&gt;Tears of the Kingdom&lt;/b&gt; &gt; &lt;b&gt;Abrir Pasta de Mods&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Extrai o zip lá dentro. Tem que ficar assim:&lt;br&gt;&lt;code&gt;.../mods/contents/0100f2c0115b6000/Sem Legenda nas Falas Dubladas/romfs/Mals/&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Botão direito no jogo &gt; &lt;b&gt;Gerenciar Mods&lt;/b&gt; e confere se tá marcado ✅&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Em &lt;b&gt;Opções &gt; Configurações &gt; Sistema&lt;/b&gt;, deixa o idioma em &lt;b&gt;Português do Brasil&lt;/b&gt; ou &lt;b&gt;Inglês Americano&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Abre o jogo e curte ?&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ol&gt;&#13;
Pra desinstalar: é só desmarcar no Gerenciar Mods (ou apagar a pasta).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;b&gt;Switch (Atmosphère):&lt;/b&gt; copia a pasta &lt;code&gt;romfs&lt;/code&gt; pra &lt;code&gt;atmosphere/contents/0100F2C0115B6000/&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Versão&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;v1.0&lt;/b&gt; - pra TOTK 1.4.3&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Créditos&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
Lista de falas dubladas baseada na dublagem PT-BR da Triforce Heroes. Ideia inspirada no mod "No Cutscene Subtitles".&lt;br&gt;Achou alguma fala dublada que ainda mostra legenda? Comenta aí com a cena que eu corrijo ?&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;</description>
      <media:content url="https://files.gamebanana.com/mods/totk_sem_legenda_falas_dubladas_v143.zip" type="application/zip"/>
      <category>Text/Dialogue</category>
      <category>UI</category>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Ordeal of the Demon King - Two New Quests</title>
      <author>- Tarnagh -</author>
      <link>https://gamebanana.com/mods/712592</link>
      <comments>https://gamebanana.com/mods/712592#PostsListModule</comments>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">c5d9dde2ccb0f6f845ee5d9f7c0820f87557592e</guid>
      <pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 14:23:43 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6aa97c7cc229e.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a9dae19baf40.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6aa97c8b8ae97.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a96fae3ed1b9.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Update:&lt;/strong&gt; v2.2.0&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Overhaul&lt;/em&gt;: new model for the Horn of the Demon King&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Improvement&lt;/em&gt;: Ganondorf's hair is now better&lt;br&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Created by &lt;strong&gt;Tarnagh&lt;/strong&gt;. Bow model and texture by &lt;strong&gt;The Hidden Yiga Clan&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Ordeal of the Demon King&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;em&gt;"You have faced monsters, Dragons, and gods. But have you ever stood before the Demon King himself?"&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Ganondorf stands, and he is waiting for you. Not for a battle - but for an answer. He has watched the bearer of the Master Sword from afar, counted his victories, and now he intends to find out for himself whether the hero is worth anything at all.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
This is a full quest line: dialogue, choices that stick, a duel of his choosing, two commissions that end with weapons no one else in Hyrule can give you - and, for those who survive him, paths no one else can open.&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;The Demon King&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
He offers you a choice.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;strong&gt;Kneel.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;strong&gt;Or refuse.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
Choose carefully. The Demon King does not offer his mercy twice.&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;The Ordeal&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Those who bow before him earn something granted to almost no one: the chance to prove themselves in single combat, against an opponent he picks personally.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
Survive, and he will admit - grudgingly, in his own way - that you are more than another hero clinging to a dying world. Refuse the duel, and the ordeal ends where it began, beneath his gaze.&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;The King's Will&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
A proven hero is a useful hero, and the Demon King has work.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
His first commission sends you after the horns of three Silver Lynels, thirty of Naydra's spikes, and a horn taken from the Light Dragon herself. Bring them, and he will forge you a bow out of them, by hand, in front of you.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;em&gt;"Watch closely as their fragile light is consumed by my darkness."&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
And the world answers him. While he forges, gloom boils up around him and the sky and earth turn the red of a Blood Moon - and when the rite is done, the colour drains away again.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
But do not mistake his favour for friendship. You serve his purpose for exactly as long as you remain useful.&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;The Horn of the Demon King&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;em&gt;"Take this. A horn of my true form. A manifestation of the doom that awaits this fragile world."&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
Come back to him carrying his bow and he will ask more of you - if you are willing to hear it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
This time he wants the horns of all three elemental Dragons, and two from the Light Dragon. What he makes of them is not a weapon but a piece of one: &lt;strong&gt;a shard of the form he has not yet taken&lt;/strong&gt;, fused from their elemental essence and his own dark magic.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Fuse it to anything you like:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;+90 attack&lt;/strong&gt; - well past anything the base game offers&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fire in every form&lt;/strong&gt; - it sets what it strikes alight, explodes in flame, keeps you warm, and does not go out&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shatters armour&lt;/strong&gt;, fells trees, and throws further&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;Shield's features: &lt;strong&gt;guard bonus, perfect-parry bonus, shield bash and counter&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
It cannot be sold. Some things are not for rupees.&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;The Demon King's Path&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;em&gt;"Name a place, then the ground between here and it will cease to matter."&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
Once his trial is behind you and his first commission given, your conversations with him can end with a request: &lt;strong&gt;open a way for me&lt;/strong&gt;. He answers with the same dark rite he forges with - and then the world folds, and you are somewhere else.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Seven places, some of them closed to you any other way:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Old Throne Room&lt;/strong&gt; - the Sanctum in Hyrule Castle&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Floating Coliseum&lt;/strong&gt; - five Lynels, and the Depths all around&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Thunderhead Isles&lt;/strong&gt; - the storm that hides the relics of the Zonai&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Imprisoning Chamber&lt;/strong&gt; - the very tomb of the prologue, where he was sealed&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Beneath Hyrule Castle&lt;/strong&gt; - Gloom's Approach, the heart of his malice&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Beneath the World&lt;/strong&gt; - below the Depths themselves, where there is nothing at all&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Western Plateau&lt;/strong&gt; - ground beyond the walls Hyrule raised to keep its world small&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
A few words of warning, because he will not give you any:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;In the &lt;strong&gt;Imprisoning Chamber&lt;/strong&gt;, do not walk on towards the Demon King's own cutscene. Leave the way you would leave anywhere else - by the map.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Beneath the World&lt;/strong&gt; means exactly that - you may arrive on gloom. Do not let it take away your life.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Features&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Demon King:&lt;/strong&gt; Ganondorf as he ought to be - imposing, calculating, merciless, and worthy of the title. His words are written in red.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Choices that stick:&lt;/strong&gt; what you say to him is remembered across saves, and he remembers it too.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The King's Trial:&lt;/strong&gt; a duel against an opponent he chooses for you, with miasma.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Two commissions:&lt;/strong&gt; hunt across Hyrule for materials no shop sells, and watch him forge them by hand - gloom, sound and a blood-red sky included.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Two unique rewards:&lt;/strong&gt; a bow of his own making, and the Horn of the Demon King.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Demon King's Road:&lt;/strong&gt; seven destinations across the surface, the sky, the Depths, and places the game never meant you to reach.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;No new NPC clutter:&lt;/strong&gt; one existing character carries the whole thing. Nothing else in the world is moved.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ol&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Installation&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TKCL / TKMM:&lt;/strong&gt; import the file and enable the mod.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manual:&lt;/strong&gt; unpack the ZIP so that &lt;code&gt;romfs&lt;/code&gt; lands in&lt;br&gt;&#13;
      &lt;code&gt;atmosphere/contents/0100F2C0115B6000/romfs/&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Emulator:&lt;/strong&gt; place the same &lt;code&gt;romfs&lt;/code&gt; folder in the game's mod directory.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Technical Specifications&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;em&gt;For developers and modders:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Host actor:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;Npc_BaseCampSoldier_Hylia005&lt;/em&gt; - renamed, re-scripted, and given Ganondorf's pack. No new actor is registered.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quest logic:&lt;/strong&gt; EventFlow, in his own flowchart - branches, talk choices, pouch queries and autosaves.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Persistence:&lt;/strong&gt; six booleans appended to &lt;em&gt;GameDataList&lt;/em&gt;, with &lt;em&gt;MetaData&lt;/em&gt; resized to match so they actually reach &lt;em&gt;progress.sav&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dialogue:&lt;/strong&gt; Mals, built from genuine vanilla 1.2.0 archives. His lines carry the inline red colour code; your choices stay white.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Teleportation:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;GameSystemActor.EventReserveBancChange&lt;/em&gt; by named start position. Two are vanilla (&lt;em&gt;OpeningStart&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;StartPos_HyruleCastleIncident&lt;/em&gt;); five are added to the &lt;em&gt;MainField&lt;/em&gt; and &lt;em&gt;MinusField&lt;/em&gt; start-position tables. The menu is three steps of four choices - the most a single talk event can show.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Custom equipment:&lt;/strong&gt; Crystallized Ice Bow (&lt;em&gt;Weapon_Bow_166_For_Ganondorf&lt;/em&gt;), Horn of the Demon King (&lt;em&gt;Item_Enemy_39&lt;/em&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Resource table:&lt;/strong&gt; every entry the mod grows is recomputed and shipped.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h3&gt;The Ordeal Awaits&lt;/h3&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;em&gt;Stand before the Demon King. Prove your worth. And remember - he is the one deciding whether you deserve to live.&lt;/em&gt;</description>
      <media:content url="https://files.gamebanana.com/mods/ordeal_of_the_demon_king_a9053.zip" type="application/zip"/>
