      <description>&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ac2dcd2a3f4f.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ac2dc7e4361c.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;Simple: both brightbloom seeds now only plant in dirt or grass.&lt;br&gt;Throw them on a different surface and the seed just bounces off!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Note: This also applies to arrow-fused seeds, but they use a different hit detection system and were really problematic and are flaky. I couldn't get the pickup-able seed item to appear on impact like the arrow itself does, so if it's a bad material hit, your seed is just gone, sorry!&lt;br&gt;On top of that, sometimes there's no bloom when there should be, sometimes there's a bloom on materials there shouldn't be... If anyone figures it out, let me know.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This forms part of the &lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/collections/209319"&gt;Cargocult Cinematic Universe&lt;/a&gt;- uh, I mean, modular gameplay reworks.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Why? Why would someone do this?!&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;This was borne out of Project Nerf The Hoverbike: when you realize that Depths darkness is permanently solved by just sticking a brightbloom onto your vehicle, you totally spoil the Depths for yourself. And the zonai devices are, officially speaking, made of stone. Now you can't do that. Mwahaha.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;But why should brightblooms stick to anything else made of stone actually? That's weird, I thought.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Anyway, this actually makes a couple areas way more interesting, like the Lightning Temple, or Zonai ruins in the depths before you hit the lightroot. You'll have to use a lit torch or a Zonai lamp on a shield. Great vibes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This mod was developed with ChatGPT 5.6 Sol using the open source &lt;a href="https://github.com/cargocult-mods/TOTK-codex-skills"&gt;TOTK modding skills&lt;/a&gt; I trained myself on my own notes.&lt;br&gt;Development of this mod took about 3 weeks of experimentation and research as side-project. There's a lot of ways to make this idea that don't work.&lt;br&gt;The released 1.0 build is development build v29.&lt;br&gt;(Wish AI was as good as AI haters think it is)</description>
