      <category>Effects</category>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Straight to Gameplay</title>
      <author>HanSoloBlaster</author>
      <link>https://gamebanana.com/mods/722493</link>
      <comments>https://gamebanana.com/mods/722493#PostsListModule</comments>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">9b7f0fb55cab0f5f12f4d0e8608f8b798b3e9fdf</guid>
      <pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 10:45:16 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6abce834cd093.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6abce8353a42e.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Straight to Gameplay&lt;/h1&gt;Skip the title screen and load your latest save automatically.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Description&lt;/h2&gt;Start the game and land in your most recent save with no button presses. After the startup logo the loading screen appears and your latest save loads. The title backdrop, the title menu, the save list and the confirmation prompt are all skipped. It is meant for people who restart the game often, such as mod developers.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Requires Tears of the Kingdom **1.2.1** and at least one save. Using without a save will probably break the game.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Installation&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Emulator:&lt;/b&gt; copy the &lt;i&gt;Straight to Gameplay&lt;/i&gt; folder into the game's mod folder&lt;br&gt;(`load/0100F2C0115B6000/`) and enable &lt;b&gt;Straight to Gameplay&lt;/b&gt; in the Add-Ons list.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Switch:&lt;/b&gt; copy the `romfs` folder from inside &lt;i&gt;Straight to Gameplay&lt;/i&gt; into&lt;br&gt;`atmosphere/contents/0100F2C0115B6000/`. Not tested on a Switch.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Resource size table:&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;Sequence/NormalTitle.module.ainb&lt;/i&gt; is larger than the original, so your&lt;br&gt;RESTBL needs updating. A mod manager (TKMM) that rebuilds the table does this for you; otherwise run a RESTBL tool after adding the mod. README.md lists the sizes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Caveats&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;br&gt;While it is enabled you cannot reach New Game, Options or an older save from the title screen, and "return to title" loads the latest save again. Disable the mod to get the menu back.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;It uses no executable module slot, patch or cheat, so it loads beside code mods. It conflicts only with mods that replace &lt;i&gt;Sequence/NormalTitle.module.ainb&lt;/i&gt; or&lt;i&gt;&amp;nbsp;Sequence/BeforeTitle.module.ainb&lt;/i&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Tested on 1.2.1 in Eden alongside several other mods.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The download contains two edited sequence graph files from the game.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Disclaimer&lt;/h2&gt;The mod was developed with the use of AI.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;</description>
      <media:content url="https://files.gamebanana.com/mods/straight-to-gameplay-v020.zip" type="application/zip"/>
      <category>Other/Misc</category>
      <category>Other/Misc</category>
    </item>
