&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;b&gt;Compatibility Issues and How to Install:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;b&gt;Mod has been tested on TOTK v.1.2.1, but other versions shouldn't be an&#13;
issue.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span class="RedColor"&gt;Important: if you have other music mods and that you downloaded the Vanilla version, make sure to place TLON ABOVE the rest of your mods! Not doing so will result in audio bugs. Remember music files do NOT merge together well, and it is heavily recommended not using several mods editing music at the same time. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;span class="RedColor"&gt;If you have issues with music mods from other creators, I unfortunately won't be able to solve them. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;br&gt;&#13;
If you don't like one of the swapped tracks or prefer the vanilla version,&lt;b&gt; feel&#13;
free to delete both the .bwav file AND the associated .bars file from the mod's&#13;
folder&lt;/b&gt;! Default music will return normally unless you use another music&#13;
mod. &lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;u&gt;Manually:&lt;/u&gt; Download the archive and extract it, then drag the mod into your Mod&#13;
Directory. &lt;br&gt;&lt;u&gt;TKMM:&lt;/u&gt; Open TKMM and download the TKCL version of your choice. Open your TKMM profile, then click on "Add Mod", and select your file. &lt;u&gt;Error messages can happen if you try to open the TKCL directly, so don't do that. &lt;/u&gt;&lt;br&gt;Place TLON above your mods if you have any other mod editing music, or below if you prefer some music of your other mods. No need to download both Vanilla and Compatible, choose just one! Once changes are done, save and launch the game. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Should I use Vanilla or Compatible? &lt;/b&gt;TLON edits tracks located in the same file as other music mods, which can result in distorted, looping or tracks cutting early. To remedy this, a Compatible version of the mod has been deployed for TKMM. &lt;u&gt;Please download the Compatible version if you have DOTK or any other music mod.&lt;/u&gt; The Vanilla version is the same as the .zip version and is unchanged (pick this one if you don't have other music mods). &lt;br&gt;The Compatible version will remove the following: Game Over, Horse Riding, Temperature tracks (Burn, Hot and Cold), Lost Woods, Battle music, Flux Construct, Dungeon Battle, Ganondorf Castle Battle, Gloom Hands (phases 1 and 2). &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;b&gt;Patch Notes:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;1.1.0: &lt;/b&gt;Overhaul of the entire soundtrack. Lowering the volume of songs so they sound less aggressive and removal of fading/silence effects to help correct looping. Added Game Over, Gerudo Underground, Lost Woods, and Flight Minigame. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1.2.0&lt;/strong&gt;: Numerous additions! 22 new songs have been added, because the multi-channel issue has been thankfully solved! The Yiga Minigame song has been updated with a new one, and Dragonhead Island song has been corrected (volume and looping). I'm proud to announce this is a huge step-up!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;TKCL: &lt;/b&gt;Now, TLON is compatible with TKMM (in vanilla and compatible) and solve compatibility issues with other music mods editing static.bars! Useful if you want to merge it with other mods like DOTK without having music sounding janky!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Compatible Bug Fix: &lt;/b&gt;The Compatible version had issues where music could be bugged or cause the game to crash when fighting Gloom Hands/Phantom Ganon and Flux Construct with DOTK on. The associated songs have been removed to avoid overlapping. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Gohma Bug Fix: &lt;/b&gt;Due to certain issues, the game was crashing when attempting to battle Marbled Gohma with TLON on! This was a critical bug that directly impacted user experience, so the music for this boss has been removed. Apologies for the removal! &lt;br&gt;In addition to this bug fix, Compatible version is now available as a .zip archive like Vanilla, and not only as a TKCL file. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Notes and Known Issues:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Loud tracks and janky transitions have been solved with the 1.1.0 patch! &lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Many thanks to Porroman420 for having suggested using another patching tool!&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;If there are any bugged tracks or a failed conversion (for ex, an in-game&#13;
track that would sound distorted, a track playing twice at once or obnoxiously&#13;
loud), please report them to me and I'll try to fix it ASAP. Don't hesitate to delete them if they&#13;
bother you. &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Due to Gamebanana's file weight limit, I had to reduce the length of a lot of the new songs in 1.2.0 (mostly the battle ones). Which can result in tracks ending a bit abruptly, even if I tried my best to preserve the mod's quality. Apologies for the inconvenience! &lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</description>
